{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002938-grappling-style-question","id":1002938,"title":"Grappling Style question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-14T10:10:47-08:00","id":1002938,"title":"Grappling Style question","content":"In the book, Grappling Style is listed as a 1-5 dot merit, but from what I can find, it only has three dots of effects listed. Is this just a typo, or am I going blind or something?<br /> <br /> Also, the third dot says you gain access to the Joint Lock move, but when looking at the different moves under Grappling, I can't seem to find this. How does this move work?<br /> <br /> There's mention of an overpowering maneuver, but again, I can't seem to find anything about this in the rules. How does an overpowering maneuver work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7004,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7004-orkonkel","user":"Orkonkel","date":". 11-14-2016, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7004-orkonkel","name":"Orkonkel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:33:13-08:00","id":1002948,"title":"","content":"It's a typo. One they fixed in the final release of the PDF, where they also changed what Joint Lock did. Now it causes bashing damage equal to your successes next turn, and can serve as a lead-in to the Restrain move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:44:41-08:00","id":1002955,"title":"","content":"How would I find the final release of the PDFs? I just downloaded the books from DriveThruRPG, so if the typo is there, I guess I don't have the right version?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7004-orkonkel","name":"Orkonkel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:46:54-08:00","id":1002958,"title":"","content":"If you look in your library there should be an updated version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:03:26-08:00","id":1002966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002938-grappling-style-question?p=1002958#post1002958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look in your library there should be an updated version.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only one I can find is from 2013-07-05 (World_of_Darkness_The_God_Machine_Chronicle.pdf ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7004-orkonkel","name":"Orkonkel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:05:02-08:00","id":1002968,"title":"","content":"Oh, you're looking at GMC? I was talking about the version in the Chronicles of Darkness book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:07:01-08:00","id":1002969,"title":"","content":"I thought the GMC book was meant to have all of the new rules and whatnot. Do I also need to purchase the Chronicles of Darkness book now?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Also, where do I find information about overpowering maneuvers in regards to grappling? It is mentioned a fair bit in merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7004,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7004-orkonkel","user":"Orkonkel","date":". 11-14-2016, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7004-orkonkel","name":"Orkonkel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:15:51-08:00","id":1002973,"title":"","content":"Well, you don't <i>need</i> it. They just fixed a typo. <br /> <br /> And added some rules on investigation and chases and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:32:39-08:00","id":1002977,"title":"","content":"Try the previews for Hurt Locker, they have a write up about Fighting Styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:35:41-08:00","id":1002981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkonkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002938-grappling-style-question?p=1002969#post1002969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the GMC book was meant to have all of the new rules and whatnot. Do I also need to purchase the Chronicles of Darkness book now?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As Elfive says, you don't need to, but <b>CofD </b>makes some tweaks (the experience cost of Integrity comes to mind), and adds a few things (like extra Merits, and the optional Fate system). It's also all integrated, rather than needing to refer back to the World of Darkness book to fill in any gaps. <i>And</i> all future blue book releases will refer to the new rulebook, rather than GMC, so there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:39:08-08:00","id":1002984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkonkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002938-grappling-style-question?p=1002969#post1002969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the GMC book was meant to have all of the new rules and whatnot. Do I also need to purchase the Chronicles of Darkness book now?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Also, where do I find information about overpowering maneuvers in regards to grappling? It is mentioned a fair bit in merits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also a reason to get the new book is that it is a stand-alone book unlike the GMC. You don't need the old 1e core book if you have the Chronicles of Darkness corebook like you do with GMC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}